   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to the adult cystic\nfibrosis assistance program",
    "basePrintNo": "S6521",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6521-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 27-G §2795, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6521\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to the adult cystic\nfibrosis assistance program\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to reimburse adults with cystic fibrosis for\ntheir health care or health insurance costs.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 2795 establishes the adult cystic fibrosis assistance program,\nwhich would reimburse the cost of providing health care or health insur-\nance to eligible individuals with cystic fibrosis. To be an eligible\nindividual for whom health care will be provided, one must be at least\n21 years old, diagnosed with cystic fibrosis, and have resided in New\nYork State for a minimum of twelve continuous months immediately prior\nto application for services, not be eligible for medical benefits under\nany group or individual health insurance policy, and not be eligible for\nmedical assistance pursuant to title 11 of article 5 of the social\nservices law solely due to earned income. All eligible individuals shall\nbe required to contribute 7% of their net annual income toward the cost\nof care and/or the cost of the health insurance premium.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCystic fibrosis (CF) is a rare genetic disease that damages the lungs\nand digestive system, which affects approximately 1600 New Yorkers.\nMany CF patients rely on several prescription drugs and targeted,\nspecific care plans for treatment.\n\nPrior to 2020, the Adult Cystic Fibrosis Assistance Program\n(ACFAP)existed as part of the annual New York State budget. ACFAP has\nhistorically provided reimbursements for out-of-pocket costs after\nenrollees spent 7% of their income on health-related expenses. These\ncosts helped enrollees to cover inpatient and outpatient care,\nprescription drugs, lab and X-ray services, home health care, and phys-\nical therapy. Enrollees in ACFAP must maintain their own healthcare\ncoverage which provides the most comprehensive coverage for their cystic\nfibrosis needs. ACFAP allows adults with CF to maintain private insur-\nance coverage and access the care and treatments required for them to\nstay healthy.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n\n\n\n\n",
